{#
  Migration 0018a/0018b — THE CLEARANCE LATTICE (ARCHITECTURE.md §5.0, §18).

  The hardest constraint in the schema, and the one the product is named after. The
  legal set of clearing verdicts is a function of ANCESTRAL severity — held in
  versioned data the customer signs, not in code we ship.

  `disposition` composite-foreign-keys to this table and `virulence` is projected onto
  the disposition from the blame closure by a trigger. The consequence is the sentence
  the company is built on: THERE IS NO DISPOSITION CONSTRUCTOR THAT DISMISSES A CONTROL
  WRITTEN BY A FATALITY. Signing one is not a warning and not a flagged event — it is
  23503, for every writer, including a DBA and including the MCP insert path.

  THREE CELLS ARE DELIBERATELY ABSENT and each is named in 0018b. Absence is the
  mechanism: a missing row in a foreign-key target is a refusal that no application
  change can route around, and the refusal names this table.

  Seed timestamps are a FIXED LITERAL, never now(). The schema-plus-seed fingerprint is
  an environment-parity gate, and a fingerprint that changes because the clock moved is
  a fingerprint that gets ignored. The value in `approved_by_sub` is 'SEED' precisely so
  that the row is visibly un-signed until a named officer of the CUSTOMER replaces it.
#}
